      "name": "definition-clarity-audit",
      "title": "definition-clarity-audit",
      "description": "Definition / statement clarity + concision audit. A content block can validate (schema-clean, refs resolve, Lean sibling present) and still read badly: the defined term is never emphasised, the definition is buried under paragraphs of motivation, or one `definition` block silently bundles three or four distinct definienda. No existing QA axis (voice / wall / q-usage / canonical / detangler / bib / proof / compute) measures clarity of the statement itself. Use when asked to \"bold defined terms\", \"tighten definitions\", \"no rambling definitions\", \"one definition per block\", \"tight theorem/proposition/lemma statements\", or to set up / run a clarity audit. Also runs the inverse audit — a non-`definition` block that secretly carries a definition (`clarity-defn-misplaced`) — plus a statement-purity check (`clarity-stmt-pure`: a theorem/prop/lemma/conjecture carries only its claim; embedded remark / interpretation moves to a follow-on `remark`) and a register check (`clarity-grad-style`: graduate-level formal-math prose — no contractions, second-person, hype, colloquialism, or emoji). Emits per-block QA sidecar params under the `clarity-*` criteria via `folio/pipeline/definition-clarity-audit.ts`.",
      "instructionsPath": "skills/local/definition-clarity-audit.md",
